comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-28T06:20:35.648Z","harness:codex","text: Duplicate check 2026-09-28: inspected the complete all-status corpus for startup, latency, entrypoint and benchmark owners and ran the live all-status CLI startup budget search. The completed transport-floor owner pm-yse5dt remains closed: its ten-sample implementation is present. The completed SDK cold-cache sampling fix is a different admission boundary and does not establish this failure mechanism. No active individual issue owns the repeated transport admission failures observed in this review. The existing scale outcome pm-o87av6 remains the parent."
  "2026-09-28T08:54:59.030Z","harness:codex","Additional live evidence 2026-09-28: during Plan receipt/evidence-note delivery, the static SDK entrypoint gate failed sdk/merge median-of-five at 240 ms against the unchanged 226 ms ceiling. Full-suite invocation-profile also exceeded its scheduling margin and two source scans hit 30-second timeouts while a separate tracker assurance scan ran; all three tests passed unchanged in a focused rerun without that competing scan. This is correlation, not causal attribution. Isolated SDK/transport reruns are pending; no performance ratchet was changed."
  "2026-09-28T09:03:00.923Z","harness:codex","Untouched-base comparison completed in a separate temporary clone at f3163466b with the same installed dependencies and Node 26.9.0. Base SDK import gate failed aggregate 514/500 ms and merge 252/226 ms; base CLI failed get 388/362, next 448/440, create 403/398 ms. Candidate isolated Node 26 rerun failed merge 232/226 and five CLI operations. Candidate Node 24.12.0 passed all 10 SDK imports; CLI failures moved to list 432/419, context 442/433, claim 425/415 ms. This confirms admission failures also exist on the unchanged base, not a clean local performance qualification. It does not identify the cause or exclude smaller regressions. Preserve all budgets; use hosted exact-head checks and continue this canonical diagnosis separately."
  "2026-10-10T18:18:22.918Z","harness:codex","Active diagnosis: capture supported runtime, pressure and bare-process controls with fresh isolated SDK/CLI transport measurements; compare unchanged base and candidate without relaxing latency/RSS budgets. A runner qualification refusal must stay unsuccessful and must never certify product admission. Historical failure causes remain unproven until controlled evidence identifies them."
  "2026-10-10T18:25:09.780Z","harness:codex","Untouched-base c233923c8a262b90dcf44de083619543d960074c isolated Node26.9.0 measurements: zero SDK or CLI budget violations. Bare Node p50 46ms/p95 51ms. CLI best get315/list323/context368/next398/create347/claim352ms; p95 values span481-660ms. Available parallelism8, load averaged2.57-2.92, free memory14.5-14.7GB. All committed latency/RSS ceilings remain unchanged. This qualifies the current base and exposes variability; it does not establish the historical failure mechanism."
  "2026-10-10T18:28:28.770Z","harness:codex","Negative-control proof: an isolated copy of the untouched base benchmark, with synthetic product observations within all budgets and bare-process medians999ms, returned successful admission without qualification. The new regression requires an explicit unsuccessful benchmark_runner_unqualified result and retains the complete report. Qualified over-budget product controls independently remain unsuccessful; no latency or RSS budget was increased."
  "2026-10-10T18:39:50.766Z","harness:codex","Candidate live pressure observation: a focused test alongside packed consumers retained zero CLI product-budget violations but bracketed bare-Node p50 controls157ms/99ms, against the unchanged106ms qualification ceiling. The gate correctly refused with benchmark_runner_unqualified and product_admission=unverified; load-average snapshots9.03/10.98 are observations, not proof of historical causation. The real measurement test uses isolated explicitly permissive fixture budgets to avoid turning a unit suite into host admission; production ceilings are unchanged."
  "2026-10-10T19:14:53.064Z","harness:codex","Candidate control classification passes the linked27-test benchmark suite and the full10111-test exact-coverage suite. Bracketed bare-process controls, complete report retention and explicit unsuccessful unqualified admission are implemented. The pressure observation and unchanged-base comparison do not identify the earlier historical overrun cause; this canonical diagnosis retains that acceptance boundary and will return open/unclaimed after delivery rather than closing a partially proven cause. All committed latency/RSS budgets are unchanged."
  "2026-10-10T19:45:25.604Z","harness:codex","The complete qualification diagnostics and public methodology are verified and closed in the execution child. Both real SDK and CLI startup gates pass on Node24 with unchanged budgets; the separate Node26 qualified merge overrun is retained. Historical failure causation remains unproven, so this diagnosis returns open and unclaimed rather than overstating the completed child."
  "2026-10-13T09:20:34.509Z","harness:codex","October13 recurrence during tracing/privacy delivery: a complete local static run fails qualified CLI transport admission at get367/362ms and create417/398ms. Standalone current-source Node26 recheck also fails create411/398ms. A separate anonymous installed published2026.10.13 artifact, using the same unchanged benchmark code and ceilings, fails all6 operations on Node26 (get423, list433, context461, next481, create453, claim460ms); bracketed bare medians53/52ms qualify under106ms. Candidate Node24.21 also records qualified latency failures with66/39ms controls. These independent baseline failures do not establish the cause or exclude a smaller regression. No source workaround, budget, margin or qualification override is used. Retain this existing diagnosis open/unclaimed and require the full hosted exact-head static gate before merge."
  "2026-10-13T11:35:19.252Z","harness:codex","Further October13 evidence: revised local static passes every gate through the10 SDK entrypoint import budgets, then qualified create misses399/398ms with bare medians46/44ms. Full local coverage execution records10381 passing tests and one scratch-lifecycle30s timeout; no coverage summary is produced, so this is not a passing coverage receipt. The unchanged lifecycle passes in the focused final-source run at4.7s alongside all124 focused checks. This does not identify historical causation. Preserve the unchanged15s lifecycle assertion and all qualification/product ceilings; require final exact-head hosted static and coverage checks."
  "2026-10-13T17:51:43.596Z","harness:codex","Current telemetry-tail source qualification on October13: complete local static processing passes dependencies, runtime inventory, docstrings, exports, unsuppressed ESLint, duplicate/workflow/package/grammar/refusal/context/registry gates and SDK surface/import costs, then the unchanged qualified CLI floor rejects get best369ms against362ms. Other five operations pass; baseline control median63ms remains qualified. Host load observations11.67 then13.49 across8 available CPUs are context, not proof of the cause or an exclusion of a small regression. Prior published-artifact comparisons remain separate; no budget or runner-admission policy is relaxed, and exact-head hosted static remains mandatory."
  "2026-10-14T17:16:09.320Z","harness:codex","Native initial PR1473 evidence at02b6dc001: Windows regression run38599081365 reports6 timing/control failures alongside3 known flag/publication expectation failures; individual30/60-second limits remain intact. The revised flag-delivery head caps the existing subprocess-heavy Windows keeper step at2 workers while preserving its complete test list, job timeout, performance budgets and platform. This is a controlled allocation change, not a proved cause or a product-admission pass; require the revised exact-head Windows check. No retry-until-green policy or qualification waiver added. Existing broad runner investigation remains open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-14T18:50:32.454Z","harness:codex","October14 final candidate local static passes every gate through the10 SDK entrypoint budgets, then qualified CLI admission rejects get388/362ms, context436/433ms, next446/440ms, create416/398ms and claim418/415ms. Bare Node26.9.0 control medians47/45ms qualify under106ms; observed load11.95→12.72 across8 CPUs is context only. This is a failed product admission, not an all-green local static receipt or a proved runner cause. Historical controlled base/publication comparisons remain separate. No budget, margin, iteration count or qualification rule changed; require the complete exact-head hosted static gate and finish the remaining local checks explicitly. Diagnosis stays open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-15T05:09:06.360Z","harness:codex","Current local candidate static reached SDK import admission, but the first benchmark was explicitly runner-unqualified: bare-Node maximum control median121ms exceeds unchanged106ms. Do not call that a product regression or pass. With no other local verification process running, a separate quiet run passes all10 SDK entrypoint budgets and its control rules without budget/margin changes. The independent CLI floor and remaining static stages are still pending, and exact-head hosted acceptance remains mandatory. Broad runner diagnosis stays open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-15T05:12:05.160Z","harness:codex","Retain the independent CLI floor result: the runner qualifies (control43/78ms below106ms), but get best374ms exceeds unchanged362ms; the other5 operations pass. This is a failed local product admission, not an unqualified result and not an all-green local static receipt. No retry or baseline increase used to erase it. Remaining correctness gates are proceeding separately; compare the immutable published baseline and require the complete exact-head hosted static gate."
  "2026-10-15T05:17:14.266Z","harness:codex","Controlled immutable comparison completed with identical current benchmark scripts and unchanged ceilings: published npm artifact2026.10.15 qualifies at49ms control and fails next445/440ms, while the frozen lifecycle candidate qualifies at46ms and passes all six operations (get336ms). This does not erase the earlier qualified candidate get374/362ms failure, establish historical causation, or exclude smaller regressions. Preserve all reports and require complete exact-head hosted static acceptance; no performance budget, margin, sample count or qualification rule changed."
  "2026-10-15T06:30:41.464Z","harness:codex","Active CI execution remediation for PR1476: immutable55bde25 Windows job exceeded its12-minute limit after the source-import/script step passed1981 tests (12 skips) in578s; the same step took464s on passing52626a. All completed subsequent steps passed, with cancellation before final native keepers. Preserve both attempts. Split scripts and native guards into two parallel Windows cohorts with the same two-worker cap and12-minute deadline; preserve every selected test and require both cohorts through a stable fail-closed Windows regression(Node24) check. This addresses serial execution occupancy, not the unproved historical runtime variability; return this broad diagnosis open/unclaimed after validation."
  "2026-10-15T06:35:52.953Z","harness:codex","Negative control rejects the old serial workflow; revised20-test workflow suite passes, including executing the aggregate shell check against success/failure/cancelled/skipped/empty outcomes. Independent before/after comparison preserves all38 selected test-path occurrences and the native release-ledger command. Typecheck, ESLint, read-only workflow permissions and docs/content-link gates pass. Initial linked run records a trust_refusal for the pre-existing command from its earlier branch; the new workflow command passed. The existing commands have been reviewed as sandbox-safe local run-tests invocations; acknowledge them for this clone without enabling untrusted execution or changing budgets."
  "2026-10-15T06:37:39.760Z","harness:codex","Both acknowledged linked commands now pass:27 runner/admission control tests and20 workflow contracts. The negative run and trust_refusal remain recorded; acknowledgement was separate and clone-local, with no untrusted-execution policy change. The two Windows cohorts retain all38 selected path occurrences and native provider acceptance; only execution topology changes, with the stable required aggregate rejecting failure/cancelled/skipped/empty results. Hosted revised-head acceptance is still required. Historical timing causation remains unproved, so return this canonical diagnosis open/unclaimed after this bounded execution fix. The updated CodSpeed report claims40.05 percent on untouched decodeQueryCursor but also flags different runtime environments and unmeasured system-call cost; do not claim a measured product improvement from that comparison."
  "2026-10-15T06:37:54.934Z","harness:codex","Evidence count correction: the current runner/admission-control command executes36 tests (18 CLI and18 SDK), not the older27-test count stated in the preceding note. Together with20 workflow contracts, both linked commands pass56 tests. Their retained stdout is authoritative; no test selection, budget or outcome changed."
  "2026-10-15T07:02:10.068Z","harness:codex","Hosted81954 preserves the original attempts and proves bounded execution: native cohort passed in254s; script cohort finished in424s, failing only the two live registry assertions because the new pipeline ID was not registered. Static and coverage shard4 fail on the same unregistered pipeline. The fail-closed required aggregate correctly refused the unsuccessful matrix. Register executable cohorts for compilation/MCP/test coverage and retain the stable aggregate as test coverage. CodeRabbit full review of81954 completed with no actionable findings; no inline threads. No deadline, test selection or policy will be relaxed."
  "2026-10-15T07:04:26.239Z","harness:codex","Registry correction passes the live registry validator and all65 linked tests:36 admission controls,20 workflow contracts and9 registry regressions. Graph composition, record integrity, terminal defect evidence and unchanged SDK surface checks pass. Compilation and MCP ownership now point to the executable cohort job; test coverage owns both cohorts and the stable required aggregate. This records a corrected integration omission, not a waiver of the failed hosted attempt. Return the broader historical investigation open/unclaimed and require all checks on the new exact head."
